    ("Joins", "When joining three tables where the join order matters for performance, what does a query optimizer generally try to do?", "Always join tables in the exact order written in the FROM clause", "Estimate the cheapest execution plan, often preferring to join smaller or more selectively filtered tables first", "Ignore table sizes entirely", "Refuse to execute multi-table joins", "B", "Query optimizers use statistics (row counts, selectivity) to choose a join order and strategy that minimizes intermediate result sizes and overall cost, rather than always following the written order."),
